.policy "ruff-n815-mixed-case-variable-in-class-scope" revision 2
.description "Name class-level variables in snake_case instead of mixedCase, as PEP 8 recommends for variable names."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N815 (pep8-naming): a name stored while Ruff's current scope is a class body, in mixedCase: not all
// lowercase, and its first letter (after one `_`) lowercase. Names are NFKC-normalised and cased by Unicode, as
// Ruff reads them. The stores are assignment, loop, `with`, walrus and `type` targets and `case` captures, including
// a walrus in a parameter default or a comprehension's first iterable, which Ruff visits in the class. Exempt:
// namedtuple/NamedTuple assignments, the fields of a TypedDict class (directly or through classes of this file), and
// names matching `pep8-naming.ignore-names`.
//   class C:
//       mixedCase = 0                 ← N815
//       match v:
//           case [fN]: ...            ← N815
//   class D(TypedDict):
//       mixedCase: bool               not reported
#include "python/python-20.rerail"

.violation N815(at: node, x: symbol) code "N815"
    "Rename the class variable `{x}` to snake_case and update its uses; keep the name if outside code depends on it or it mirrors an external schema."
    suppress ruff "N815"
N815(n, x) :- ruff_store(n, x, c), kind(c, "class_definition"), ruff_mixed(n, x), !store_makes(n, "namedtuple"),
    !typed_dict(c), !ruff_ignored(n, x).
// typed_dict(c): class c derives from TypedDict, at any depth (python/names' class_anc, by its own module's rows:
// scopes' subclass, a table of every file's classes, put c in the cross-file part, decision 0677).
.decl typed_dict(c: node)
typed_dict(c) :- class_anc(c, b), (b = "typing.TypedDict" ; b = "typing_extensions.TypedDict").
